{title: No, Not One}
{artist: Johnson Oatman & George Hugg}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
There's [G]not a friend like the [C]lowly [G]Jesus — [C]no, not [G]one! [D]No, not [G]one!
None else could heal [C]all our [G]souls' diseases — [C]no, not [G]one! [D]No, not [G]one!

Chorus
[C]Jesus knows [G]all about our struggles, [D]he will guide till the [G]day is done:
there's [G]not a friend like the [C]lowly [G]Jesus — [C]no, not [G]one! [D]No, not [G]one!

Verse 2
No friend [G]like Him is so high and holy, No, not one! [C]no, not [G]one! And yet [C]no friend is so [G]meek and [D]lowly, No, not one! [G]no, not
one! Jesus knows all about our struggles, He [C]will guide till the [G]day is done; There's not [C]a friend like the [G]lowly Jesus, [D]No, not one! no, [G]not one!

Verse 3
There's not [G]an hour that He is not near us, No, not [C]one! no, [G]not one! No night [C]so dark but His [G]love can [D]cheer us, No, not [G]one! no,
not one! Jesus knows all about our struggles, [C]He will guide till [G]the day is done; There's not [C]a friend like the [G]lowly Jesus, [D]No, not one! no, [G]not one!

Verse 4
Did ever [G]saint find this friend forsake him? No, not one! no, [C]not one! [G]Or sinner find [C]that He would not [G]take him? [D]No, not one! no, [G]not one!
Jesus knows all about our struggles, He [C]will guide till the [G]day is done; There's not a [C]friend like the lowly [G]Jesus, [D]No, not one! no, [G]not one!

Verse 5
Was e'er [G]a gift like the Savior given? No, not one! [C]no, not [G]one! Will He refuse [C]us a home in [G]heaven? [D]No, not one! no, [G]not one!
Jesus knows all about our struggles, He [C]will guide till the [G]day is done; There's not a [C]friend like the lowly [G]Jesus, [D]No, not one! no, [G]not one!
